<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<RSLogix5000Content SchemaRevision="1.0" SoftwareRevision="16.03" TargetType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" ContainsContext="true" Owner="Dale Reed, Rockwell Automation" ExportDate="Fri Jul 31 10:47:47 2009" ExportOptions="References Context">
<Controller Use="Context" Name="ProcessObjix">
<DataTypes Use="Context">
<DataType Name="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY" Family="NoFamily" Class="User">
<Description>
<![CDATA[UDT containing a 64-bit (LINT-sized) BOOL array for use as a COP destination]]>
</Description>
<Members>
<Member Name="Bit" DataType="BOOL" Dimension="64" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Bit array]]>
</Description>
</Member>
</Members>
</DataType>
</DataTypes>
<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_OTU" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="00 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2009-07-07T16:39:50.037Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2009-07-31T14:47:35.372Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output Unlatch (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Initial Release]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction unlatches the given Bit of the referenced LINT (64-bit integer)
tag, that is, it clears the given bit (false, 0) if the EnableIn condition is TRUE, or
leaves the given bit (and the referenced LINT) unmodified if the EnableIn
condition is FALSE.

If the given Bit number is outside the range 0..63, the controller will
MAJOR FAULT on an invalid array index (bad bit number). To keep
performance "snappy", there is no validity checking of the given Bit number!]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="Ref_LINT" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[LINT in which to set/clear a bit]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_BitNum" DataType="DINT" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Bit position to examine (0 .. 63)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output (for visible animation)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Bit" DataType="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Array of 64 BOOLs (must be in a UDT to COPy to it)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, ONLY reflect the state of the selected bit in "Out" (for animation)]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
===================================================
When EnableIn is false, an OTU "does nothing" -- but the "Out" (output) bit
is displayed for animation, and it needs to reflect the actual state of the selected bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_LINT,Wrk_Bit,1)XIC(Wrk_Bit.Bit[Inp_BitNum])OTE(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is true, clear selected bit and "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_OTU : 64-bit Output Unlatch
============================================================
Revision 1.0-00 Release:  2009-Jun-31
Initial Release
============================================================
This instruction unlatches the given Bit of the referenced LINT (64-bit integer)
output, that is, it clears the bit (false, 0) if the EnableIn condition is TRUE, or
leaves the bit (and the referenced LINT) unmodified if the EnableIn condition is FALSE.

If the given Bit number is outside the range 0..63, the controller will
MAJOR FAULT on an invalid array index (bad bit number). To keep
performance "snappy", there is no validity checking of the given Bit number!

Logix (V16/V17) has a LINT data type, but bit instructions
(and AOI Input and Output Parameters) don't support LINT.

This version of the L_OTU instruction:

*  copies the referenced LINT into a 64-bit BOOL array
(This must be done with a UDT -- you can't COPy to
a BOOL array -- so there is a dependency on an
external type definition -- UDT!)

*  does NO checking of the bit number
(If the bit number is not in the range 0 to 63, the
controller will fault on an invalid array index!)

* unlatches the appropriate bit in the array (to 0) if EnableIn is true.
(It does NOTHING if EnableIn is false.)

* copies the BOOL array back to the LINT reference

NOTE: to do this without copying over other references to
the LINT (say, in other Tasks), we must use a UID/UIE block!
===================================================
CONVERT LINT TO BOOL [ array ]
===================================================
This COPy takes the input LINT and copies it into a BOOL array.
NOTE:  a BOOL array must be placed inside a UDT to do a COPy to it!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[UID()COP(Ref_LINT,Wrk_Bit,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
UNLATCH THE GIVEN BIT IN THE ARRAY
===================================================
Unlatch the bit in the BOOL [ 64 ] array.
In this case, EnableIn is true, so the given bit is CLEARED.

The Output bit follows the actual bit -- it is used for
animation of the ladder display.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_Bit.Bit[Inp_BitNum])OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CONVERT UPDATED BOOL [ array ] BACK TO LINT
===================================================
This COPy takes the modified BOOL array and copies it
back into the Referenced LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Wrk_Bit,Ref_LINT,1)UIE();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
